; Plan 39 export fixture: securities written as QIF investment registers.
;
; assets:broker is one Invst register: its sub-accounts hold securities plus
; one cash account. assets:ira holds its cash and its shares in the one
; account, so it is a register of its own. Covered: buys from the
; brokerage's cash and from checking, a commission, a partial sell, a full
; sell with a realized-gain posting, a dividend marked with a zero-unit
; posting, a dividend paid to checking, interest with no security, a
; reinvested dividend, a security transferred in from equity, shares moved in
; kind between registers, and P prices (plus one exchange rate, which QIF
; cannot carry).

account assets:bank:checking    ; type: C
account assets:bank:euro        ; type: C
account assets:broker           ; type: A
account assets:broker:cash      ; type: C
account assets:broker:aapl      ; type: A
account assets:broker:vti       ; type: A
account assets:broker:fund      ; type: A
account assets:ira              ; type: A
account income:dividends        ; type: R
account income:interest         ; type: R
account income:gains            ; type: R
account expenses:fees           ; type: X
account expenses:travel         ; type: X
account equity:opening          ; type: E
account equity:transfers        ; type: E

commodity $1,000.00
commodity 1.000,00 EUR
commodity 1.000 AAPL
commodity 1.00 VTI
commodity 1.000 FXAIX  ; name: Fidelity 500 Index Fund, type: mutualfund

P 2024-03-28 AAPL $171.48
P 2024-03-28 FXAIX $182.10
P 2024-06-28 AAPL $210.62
P 2024-06-28 VTI $259.40
P 2024-06-28 FXAIX $191.50
P 2024-06-28 EUR $1.07

